  "interpretation_caveat": "Sentinel-2 sample is cloud-filtered (<20% cover), which excludes ~93% of rainy-season scenes (0 of 40 sampled scenes were from June/July). This field is a DRY-SEASON optical baseline, not a flood-season cross-check -- SAR-S2 spatial correlation was ~0 (r=-0.07) because the two sensors sample different seasonal populations, not because either is wrong. Do not read this as a validated QA agreement signal.",
  "conclusion": "Sentinel-2/MNDWI cross-validation for FLOODS is not viable with a simple cloud-filtered approach -- the cloud filter removes the rainy season. Parked per team decision (2026-08). Sentinel-2 remains a strong candidate for a future FIRE detection module, where clear-sky bias is not a problem."
